// ch01 (round 2, R2-1): `vibe run` demands an executable root -- on a
// plain .vibe, even one with a valid `main`, the launcher refuses
// before compiling anything. The run directive reproduces it:
//   vibe: vibe run requires a .vibex executable root: <this file>
// (exit 1). The compile lane below still compiles and runs this file
// normally -- the restriction is the run verb's, not the language's.
//! cli: run
fn main with Console {
  println("plain .vibe with main")
}
